runsc: give the containers' oom_score_adj to the stubs, not the Sentry or gofer

What: runsc gives the containers' oom_score_adj (when a container starts, and
again when one leaves a multi-container sandbox) to the platform's stubs, the
children of the sandbox process, which run the application. The Sentry and
each container's gofer get it only where it is below the value the sandbox
inherited; on a platform without stubs the Sentry gets it as before.

runsc finds the stubs in /proc/<pid>/task/<tid>/children, which the Host
kernel has only with CONFIG_PROC_CHILDREN. Without it runsc finds none and
logs nothing: the Sentry gets the containers' value as before, the stubs keep
the inherited one, and each gofer still gets it only where it is lower, so
under rootful Docker a container that exceeds --memory loses the whole
sandbox, as with stock runsc.

Why: under rootful Docker, a container that exceeded --memory lost the whole
sandbox. The Sentry forks the first stub at boot and clones every later stub
from it, so the stubs kept the -998 of containerd's runc shim while the Sentry
got the container's 0, and the OOM killer chose the Sentry. Giving the stubs 0
as well is not enough: the application's memory lives in the Sentry's memory
file and is mostly not mapped in any stub, so the Sentry's resident set (about
50 MB) is often the largest and the Sentry is still chosen. The gofer,
about 11 MB resident, is likewise chosen before any stub that maps less, and
the sandbox cannot serve the container's files without it. Kept at the
inherited value, both leave the OOM killer the stub that maps the most memory,
normally the allocating process's, and only that process dies, as under runc.

Under rootless Docker the inherited value is one above the user's containerd
(1 where it runs at 0), and an unprivileged process cannot go below its
oom_score_adj_min, the value its user's systemd manager started with, so with
Docker's default the Sentry, the gofer and the stubs tie. A container
oom_score_adj above the inherited value (docker run --oom-score-adj) puts the
stubs ahead of them there too. Memory written into a tmpfs in the sandbox with
write(2) is mapped by the Sentry itself, so filling the limit that way still
ends the sandbox.

Verified, in containers run with --memory 512m --memory-swap 512m in which one
process writes a heartbeat every second while another uses memory:
- Rootful Docker 29.1.3 (cgroup v2, kernel 7.0), a process allocating 1.5 GB.
  Stock runsc (stubs -998, Sentry 0) lost the whole container, and so did
  stubs given the Sentry's 0. With this patch (Sentry, gofer and FD-parking sidecar -998,
  stubs 0) the kernel killed the allocating stub, the allocator exited with 137
  and the heartbeat kept running, in 3 runs of 3.
- The same, a process filling /dev/shm through mmap 50 MB at a time and
  unmapping each part, so that little of the memory is mapped: the kernel
  killed the writer's stub (about 2800 resident pages, the gofer about 2950)
  and the heartbeat kept running, in 3 runs of 3, as under runc. With the
  gofer set to the container's 0 by hand, it killed the gofer and the
  container exited with 137.
- The same, dd filling /dev/shm: the kernel killed the Sentry at -998, which
  mapped 500 MB of it, and the container exited with 137, in 2 runs of 2.
  Under runc it killed the heartbeat and dd, and the shell went on.
- Rootless Docker 29.9.3 (systemd cgroup driver, cgroup v2, kernel 5.15), with
  --oom-score-adj 500 (stubs 500, Sentry, gofer and FD-parking sidecar 1):
  only the allocator died in 4 runs of 4, and only the mmap writer in 2 of 2.
  With Docker's default 0 the allocator, which mapped more than the Sentry,
  died alone in 3 runs of 3, but the mmap writer took the whole container in
  2 of 2.

gVisor's root tests TestOOMScoreAdjSingle and TestOOMScoreAdjMulti
(test/root/oom_score_adj_test.go) still expect the container's value on the
Sentry and the gofer; Orbit's build does not run them.

diff --git a/runsc/container/container.go b/runsc/container/container.go
index 3b80cd4..6773449 100644
--- a/runsc/container/container.go
+++ b/runsc/container/container.go
@@ -581,8 +581,8 @@ func (c *Container) startImpl(conf *config.Config, action string, startRoot func
 		return err
 	}
 
-	// Set container's oom_score_adj to the gofer since it is dedicated to
-	// the container, in case the gofer uses up too much memory.
+	// Set container's oom_score_adj to the gofer, unless the sandbox inherited
+	// a lower one.
 	return c.adjustGoferOOMScoreAdj()
 }
 
@@ -2240,12 +2240,17 @@ func (c *Container) IsSandboxRoot() bool {
 }
 
 // adjustGoferOOMScoreAdj sets the oom_store_adj for the container's gofer.
+//
+// Like the Sentry, the gofer gets the container's value only where it is below
+// the value the sandbox inherited. The sandbox cannot serve the container's
+// files without it, so the OOM killer must not choose it; with the stubs' value
+// it would, as soon as no stub maps more memory than the gofer holds.
 func (c *Container) adjustGoferOOMScoreAdj() error {
 	goferPid := c.GoferPid.Load()
 	if goferPid == 0 || c.Spec.Process.OOMScoreAdj == nil {
 		return nil
 	}
-	return setOOMScoreAdj(goferPid, *c.Spec.Process.OOMScoreAdj)
+	return setOOMScoreAdj(goferPid, min(*c.Spec.Process.OOMScoreAdj, c.Sandbox.OriginalOOMScoreAdj))
 }
 
 // adjustSandboxOOMScoreAdj sets the oom_score_adj for the sandbox.
@@ -2314,8 +2319,77 @@ func adjustSandboxOOMScoreAdj(s *sandbox.Sandbox, spec *specs.Spec, rootDir stri
 		return nil
 	}
 
-	// Set the lowest of all containers oom_score_adj to the sandbox.
-	return setOOMScoreAdj(s.Getpid(), lowScore)
+	// Set the lowest of all containers oom_score_adj to the processes that run
+	// them.
+	return setApplicationOOMScoreAdj(s.Getpid(), lowScore, containers[0].Sandbox.OriginalOOMScoreAdj)
+}
+
+// setApplicationOOMScoreAdj gives scoreAdj to the processes that run the
+// application: the platform's stubs, which are the children of the sandbox
+// process, or the sandbox process itself on a platform without stubs. The
+// kernel gives a stub's value to every process that shares its address space,
+// such as systrap's sysmsg threads.
+//
+// With stubs, the sandbox process, the Sentry, gets scoreAdj only where it is
+// below original, the value the Sentry inherited from its parent, so that the
+// kernel's OOM killer chooses a stub before the Sentry. Under containerd's runc
+// shim the Sentry thus keeps -998, like the shim. The application's memory
+// lives in the Sentry's memory file and little of it is mapped in any stub at a
+// time, so the Sentry has the largest resident set in the container's cgroup:
+// with the stubs' value, it would be the one killed when the container exceeds
+// its memory limit, and every process with it. Held back, it leaves the OOM
+// killer the stub that maps the most memory, normally the one allocating, and
+// only that application process dies, as under runc.
+func setApplicationOOMScoreAdj(pid, scoreAdj, original int) error {
+	if len(childProcesses(pid)) == 0 {
+		return setOOMScoreAdj(pid, scoreAdj)
+	}
+	if err := setOOMScoreAdj(pid, min(scoreAdj, original)); err != nil {
+		return err
+	}
+	// The Sentry forks the first stub at boot, before this runs, and clones
+	// every later stub from it, so a stub inherits the value its source has
+	// when it is cloned. Repeat until a pass finds no stub it has not set.
+	set := make(map[int]bool)
+	for pass := 0; pass < 10; pass++ {
+		found := false
+		for _, stub := range childProcesses(pid) {
+			if set[stub] {
+				continue
+			}
+			set[stub] = true
+			found = true
+			if err := setOOMScoreAdj(stub, scoreAdj); err != nil {
+				return err
+			}
+		}
+		if !found {
+			return nil
+		}
+	}
+	return nil
+}
+
+// childProcesses returns the PIDs of the child processes of every thread of
+// the given process.
+func childProcesses(pid int) []int {
+	tasks, err := os.ReadDir(fmt.Sprintf("/proc/%d/task", pid))
+	if err != nil {
+		return nil
+	}
+	var children []int
+	for _, task := range tasks {
+		data, err := os.ReadFile(fmt.Sprintf("/proc/%d/task/%s/children", pid, task.Name()))
+		if err != nil {
+			continue
+		}
+		for _, field := range strings.Fields(string(data)) {
+			if child, err := strconv.Atoi(field); err == nil {
+				children = append(children, child)
+			}
+		}
+	}
+	return children
 }
 
 // setOOMScoreAdj sets oom_score_adj to the given value for the given PID.
